      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n\n## Column Mapping\n- courses: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER\n- Mathematics department: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- average for Mathematics department courses in the same academic year: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- course number: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- subject title: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- row number within each academic year group ordered by course number: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- degree-granting department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject code: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE\n- subject code description: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC\n- average ASCII value of course number: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- variance of ASCII value of course number: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For courses offered by the Mathematics department with at least 5 enrolled students, show the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, and assign row numbers within each academic year group ordered by course number.\n```sql\nSELECT t0.COURSE_NUMBER, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t0.COURSE_NUMBER) AS window_column FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 5\n```\n2. For each department, provide the department name and calculate the average and variance of the department's subject codes' course numbers (using their ASCII values), considering only departments that are degree granting.\n```sql\nSELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(ASCII(s.COURSE_NUMBER)) AS avg_course_number_ascii, VARIANCE(ASCII(s.COURSE_NUMBER)) AS var_course_number_ascii FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT d JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY var_course_number_ascii DESC;\n```\n3. For courses offered by the Mathematics department with at least 5 enrolled students, show the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, and assign row numbers within each academic year group ordered by course number, but only include those courses where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average number of enrolled students for Mathematics department courses in the same academic year.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t0.COURSE_NUMBER, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t0.COURSE_NUMBER) AS window_column FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 5 ), avg_enrollment AS ( SELECT t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR, AVG(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_students FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 5 GROUP BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR ) SELECT i.COURSE_NUMBER, i.SUBJECT_TITLE, i.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, i.TERM_DESCRIPTION, i.ACADEMIC_YEAR, i.window_column FROM inner_cte i JOIN avg_enrollment a ON i.ACADEMIC_YEAR = a.ACADEMIC_YEAR WHERE i.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > a.avg_students;\n```\n4. For each degree-granting department, list the department name, the subject code, the subject code description, and the average and variance of the ASCII values of the course numbers for that subject code.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.SUBJECT_CODE, s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, s.COURSE_NUMBER FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT d JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' ) SELECT inner_cte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, inner_cte.SUBJECT_CODE, inner_cte.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, AVG(ASCII(inner_cte.COURSE_NUMBER)) AS avg_course_number_ascii, VARIANCE(ASCII(inner_cte.COURSE_NUMBER)) AS var_course_number_ascii FROM inner_cte GROUP BY inner_cte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, inner_cte.SUBJECT_CODE, inner_cte.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC ORDER BY var_course_number_ascii DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor courses offered by the Mathematics department with at least 5 enrolled students, where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average for Mathematics department courses in the same academic year, show the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, and the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number. For each such course, also show the name of the degree-granting department, the subject code, the subject code description, and the average and variance of the ASCII values of the course numbers for that subject code, listing the columns in this order: course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, row number, department name, subject code, subject code description, average ASCII value of course number, and variance of ASCII value of course number. Do not return any rounded answers."
